# Calibration & Warm-Up Notes

> [!WARNING]
> **Warm-Up Phase**: MQ-series sensors contain an internal heating element. On initial start, they will draw high currents and read highly unstable values. Always allow a warm-up phase of at least 3 to 5 minutes before trusting sensor outputs.
>
> **Tuning**: Use the small potentiometer on the back of the MQ-2 module to set its digital switching sensitivity, ensuring it changes state correctly when exposed to small smoke samples.
